WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.274
Hi! Is the ball in the box or on it? Do we go to school on Monday or in the morning? Today we'll learn prepositions of place and time.

2
00:00:11.424 --> 00:00:14.322
In means inside: in the box.

3
00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:17.322
On means on top: on the table.

4
00:00:17.472 --> 00:00:20.442
Under means below: under the chair.

5
00:00:20.592 --> 00:00:26.442
Behind is at the back, in front of is ahead, next to is beside.

6
00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:29.754
Clock times take at: at 8 o'clock.

7
00:00:29.904 --> 00:00:32.322
Days take on: on Monday.

8
00:00:32.472 --> 00:00:34.794
Months take in: in May.

9
00:00:34.944 --> 00:00:39.906
We say in the morning and in the afternoon, but at night.

10
00:00:40.056 --> 00:00:43.938
Watch out! We don't use in before days!

11
00:00:44.088 --> 00:00:46.578
Days take on: on Sunday.

12
00:00:46.728 --> 00:00:50.346
Months take in: in June.

13
00:00:50.496 --> 00:01:01.122
Your turn! The cat is, ___, the box. It's inside. Which one? Pause and think.

14
00:01:01.272 --> 00:01:06.090
Inside means in. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:16.938
Another one! The book is, ___, the desk. It's on top. Which one? Pause and think.

16
00:01:17.088 --> 00:01:21.858
On top means on. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:22.008 --> 00:01:32.562
Here's another! The ball is, ___, the bed. It's below. Which one? Pause and think.

18
00:01:32.712 --> 00:01:37.458
Below means under. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:37.608 --> 00:01:48.594
Try one more! School starts, ___, 7.30. Which one? Pause and think.

20
00:01:48.744 --> 00:01:53.706
Clock times take at. Did you get it right?

21
00:01:53.856 --> 00:02:03.546
Try one more! My birthday is, ___, March. Which one? Pause and think.

22
00:02:03.696 --> 00:02:08.250
Months take in. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:17.658
Try one more! We have art, ___, Friday. Which one? Pause and think.

24
00:02:17.808 --> 00:02:22.410
Days take on. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:33.330
Try one more! Tom sits, ___, Mei. He's beside her. Which one? Pause and think.

26
00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:38.610
Beside means next to. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:48.114
Last one! My birthday is, ___, May. Which one? Pause and think.

28
00:02:48.264 --> 00:02:52.817
Months take in. Did you get it right?

29
00:02:52.968 --> 00:03:00.498
Remember: in is inside, on is on top, under is below. Use at for times, on for days and in for months.

30
00:03:00.648 --> 00:03:04.169
Say where your toys are!

